A||||4||Firebug||Aluminum cooling tubes||||1||
Z||000000||Firebug||03-01-2001||01:58 AM||||I'm converting from a 2.5 to a 2.8 and I stripped a car that had a 2.8.  There were these aluminum cooling tubes that went into the luggage compartment behind the motor.  They looked like aluminum pipes with flanges that bolted to the firewall.  I believe that they were intended for cooling.  Do I need these???  If so, do I need to do something with duct work under the carpet???  Any help will be appreciated.<BR> <BR>Thanks, <P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||03-01-2001||06:33 AM||||You need the tail light wiring harness, (for the fan wiring) the engine cooling fan (located in the pass. side of trunk), trunk carpet and the plastic duct work under the carpet closest to the engine. And of course the tubes you saw.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||03-01-2001||10:27 AM||||theres a fan in the pass side qtr panel, it goes into the bulkhead between the engine and rear storage (its hollow). those tubes bold over holes in it to cool the ignition coil and the alternator diodes. I think in 88 they put a heat absorbing pad on those and eliminated the blower.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheFiero64||03-01-2001||10:36 AM||||I don't think you need them. The 88's don't have them. It is always good to have as much cooling affect as possible, but it may be hard to swap the system in.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Johnson's85SE||03-01-2001||01:21 PM||||Hi,<BR>  I belive you are talking about the recall. There was a tube that ran threw the firewall into the air intake. It was a fire hazard, So they recalled it, on the V6's. I have it on mine, the tube just hangs there not connected to anything.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Chris in Calgary<BR>||||reg||1
